I'm not sure where you got that list from, I clicked around for a bit
but couldn't find it. I'm interested to see the numbers myself.

I did see this, however:
http://alt.org/nethack/statnethack/statnethack.txt

And I noticed that Cav is by far the LEAST played class. I'm not sure
how that affects your interpretation of the numbers (if at all) since
you were only looking at the top 200 ascenders, but it seems to me
that if most of the people playing Cav are not playing it as one of
their first even three ascensions, the ascension percentage would
obviously be much higher... not surprisingly, even though I played 191
games on nao, 6 of my ascensions were in the last 18 games, which also
includes 3 quits, of which one was a mistype when selecting role and
two were accidentally breaking vegan as a monk. So if most people have
perhaps not exactly the same experience, they likely have one similar
enough that if they saved Cav towards the end of their nethack careers
they are much more likely to ascend it. Tourist, on the other hand, in
my random guesswork opinion, has a reputation of being "the most
difficult" class, so people are more likely to try it as a result
earlier in their nethack career.

